#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:57
msgid "Cloud-Init"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:59
msgid ""
"To get started with a base CentOS image we first install cloud-init. This"
" is a relatively simple process using yum:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:61
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"yum -y install epel-release\n"
"yum -y install git wget ntp curl cloud-init dracut-modules-growroot\n"
"rpm -qa kernel | sed 's/^kernel-//'  | xargs -I {} dracut -f "
"/boot/initramfs-{}.img {}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:67
msgid ""
"There are two parts to this yum installation. We are first ensuring some "
"core dependencies are installed for automation as well as cloud-init. git"
" for example is installed for use by ansible playbook automation down the"
" line and is therefore optional if not using ansible. The dracut-modules-"
"growroot is responsible for resizing the root partition upon first boot "
"to match the virtual disk size that was potentially adjusted during "
"provisioning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:69
msgid ""
"A great benefit to using cloud-init is credentials don't have to be "
"locked into the blueprint. It is advisable, within |morpheus| , to "
"configure the default cloud-init user that gets created when the vm boots"
" automatically by cloud-init. This is located in "
":menuselection:`Administration --> Settings --> Provisioning`, within the"
" Cloud-Init Settings section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:72
#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:135
msgid "Network Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:74
msgid ""
"A slightly annoying change with centOS 7 is that the network interfaces "
"have changed naming convention. You may notice when running ifconfig that"
" the primary network interface is set to something like ens2344 or some "
"other random number. This naming is dynamic typically by hardware id and "
"we don't want this to fluctuate when provisioning the blueprint in "
"various VMware environments. Fortunately, there is a way to turn this "
"functionality off and restore the interface back to eth0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:76
msgid ""
"Firstly we need to adjust our bootloader to disable interface naming like"
" this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:78
msgid ""
"sed -i -e 's/quiet/quiet net.ifnames=0 biosdevname=0/' /etc/default/grub\n"
"grub2-mkconfig -o /boot/grub2/grub.cfg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:84
msgid ""
"The above command adds a few arguments to the kernel args list (namely "
"``net.ifnames=0`` and ``biosdevname=0``. It may be useful to view the "
"``/etc/default/grub`` file and ensure these settings were indeed applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:86
msgid ""
"The next step is to adjust the network-scripts in centOS. we need to "
"ensure we have a file called ``/etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ifcfg-"
"eth0``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:88
msgid ""
"Below is a script that we run on our packer builds to prepare the "
"machines network configuration files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:90
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"export iface_file=$(basename \"$(find /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ "
"-name 'ifcfg*' -not -name 'ifcfg-lo' | head -n 1)\")\n"
"export iface_name=${iface_file:6}\n"
"echo $iface_file\n"
"echo $iface_name\n"
"sudo mv /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/$iface_file /etc/sysconfig"
"/network-scripts/ifcfg-eth0\n"
"sudo sed -i -e \"s/$iface_name/eth0/\" /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts"
"/ifcfg-eth0\n"
"sudo bash -c 'echo NM_CONTROLLED=\\\"no\\\" >> /etc/sysconfig/network-"
"scripts/ifcfg-eth0'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:101
msgid ""
"This script tries to ensure there is a new ifcfg-eth0 config created to "
"replace the old ens config file. Please do verify this config exists "
"after running. If it does not you will have to be sure to build one on "
"your own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/vmware/vmware_templates.rst:103
msgid ""
"TYPE=Ethernet\n"
"DEVICE=eth0\n"
"NAME=eth0\n"
"ONBOOT=yes\n"
"NM_CONTROLLED=\"no\"\n"
"BOOTPROTO=\"dhcp\"\n"
"DEFROUTE=yes"
msgstr ""

